// expect_error: 14:1 belongs to the standard library and is not available in profile 'kernel'
// expect_error_count: 1
// tests/neg/kernel_std_io.fi -- ROUND 73: WHAT STAYS FORBIDDEN.
//
// Round 73 opened `import std.core` for the kernel profile. This test
// nails down that it opened nothing else: `std.io` presumes SYS_WRITE and
// SYS_READ, and below a freestanding kernel there is no operating system
// that could take them. The message is the one round 52 wrote; the rule
// became more precise, not milder.
//
// The counter-part -- a module that CLAIMS `profile kernel` and allocates
// all the same -- stands in tests/neg/kernel_liar.fi.
profile kernel
import std.io

fn kmain() -> i32 {
    return 0
}
